course: dictionary
lesson: 10904
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word vision has more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Her vision is blurred, so the board looks fuzzy.» Here vision means your ability to see, your eyesight.
explain: «Her vision for the school was a garden on every roof.» This vision is a picture in her mind of what the school could be like in the future: a plan or a dream.
explain: «The bike came out of my vision.» Here vision means the area you can see. Try each meaning in the sentence. Does it still make sense? Then you have found the right one.
fact: Vision means your ability to see, or your eyesight.
fact: A vision is a picture in your mind of what something could be like in the future, like a plan or a dream.
fact: «Blurred vision» means seeing things fuzzy and unclear.
fact: «Peripheral vision» means seeing things at the sides, which helps you spot movement.
fact: Carrots help your eyes only if you lack vitamin A; they do not give you night vision.
exercise: «Her vision is blurred, so the board looks fuzzy.» What does vision mean here? | A dream you have at night | A long, thin stick | *Your ability to see, your eyesight | A picture of the future
exercise: «He had a vision of a city in the sky.» What does a vision mean here? | Your eyes being tested | The area you can see | *A picture in your mind of what could be in the future | A loud noise
exercise: Side vision is also called what? | *Peripheral vision | Night vision | Blurred vision | Good vision
test: Do carrots give you night vision? | *No, they help eyes only if you lack vitamin A | Only in winter | Yes, always | Yes, if you eat ten a day
test: «An optometrist tests your vision with a letter chart.» What does an optometrist test with the chart? | Your shoes | Your teeth | Your height | *Your vision
exam: In the words «out of my vision», what does vision mean? | *The area I can see | A bright light | My eyesight test | A dream about the future
